        "title": "Fossil Fuels and the Transition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Fossil fuels still supply ~80% of global primary energy and will continue to for decades.\nThe transition is not a switch — it's a multi-decade replacement of capital stock with\n50-year lifetimes. Understanding the transition requires understanding stranded assets,\ncarbon capture as bridge technology, methane leakage as the sleeper problem, and the\npolitical economy of communities whose economies depend on what must go away."
